{"version":"1","id":"adam-bien","handle":"adam-bien","name":"Adam Bien","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--CInnAL-q--/f_auto,q_auto/v1773644276/logos/adam-bien?_a=BAMAMiiu0","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-4.4427,"y":-5.3591,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":19,"newest_post_at":"2026-05-04T12:02:44.197Z","oldest_post_at":"2026-03-16T06:58:01.741Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":1.210526,"summary_length_avg":369.736842,"title_length_avg":16.0,"title_length_var":0.0,"tag_entropy":2.556172,"tag_diversity":1.210526,"top_tag_share":0.578947,"avg_upvotes":0.0,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.0,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":1.0,"zero_engagement_share":1.0,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":2.702615,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":19.0},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-9.9853,-9.9559],"cadence_depth":[-8.4265,-8.9118],"hype_variety":[-9.8529,-6.0147],"title_style":[-9.9118,-9.8088]},"top_tags":[["java",19],["quarkus",7],["serverless",4],["aws",3],["aws-lambda",3],["mcp",2],["jakarta-ee",2],["testing",2]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["adam bien's blog","adam bien's blog","adam bien's blog"],"outlier":[]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"kns2p58dY","title":"adam bien's blog","url":"https://adambien.blog/roller/abien/entry/rust_sse_websockets_bce_jpa_history_llms_questions_and_","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/adam-bien-s-blog-kns2p58dy","summary":"Adam Bien announces the 146th airhacks.tv Q&A session covering topics including Rust programming language opinions, SSE, WebSockets, BCE, JPA historization, and LLMs. The session also revisits past episodes from 2017-2018 covering Java EE metrics, Kotlin, JWT authentication, and more. The live Q&A runs monthly on the first Monday at 8 PM.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d365e8cabb5d95ba36aaa092c23f211d?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-04T12:02:44.197Z"},{"id":"UJH3ijtjO","title":"adam bien's blog","url":"https://adambien.blog/roller/abien/entry/live_coding_at_devoxx_greece_your_java_code_is_your_llm_prompt","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/adam-bien-s-blog-ujh3ijtjo","summary":"zunit is a zero-dependency, single-file test runner for Java 25 that discovers *Test.java files and runs them directly via `java --source 25`. No compilation step, no JUnit, and no build tool are required. Each test is a self-contained script with a `void main()` method, and each test gets its own JVM for full execution isolation. It supports auto-detection of tests, explicit classpath configuration, and integration with the zb build tool.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d365e8cabb5d95ba36aaa092c23f211d?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-03T07:01:56.388Z"},{"id":"15Pa9lpQA","title":"adam bien's blog","url":"https://adambien.blog/roller/abien/entry/_hello_world_java_25_script_in_4_lines","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/adam-bien-s-blog-15pa9lpqa","summary":"Java 25 introduces source-file mode that lets you run a single Java file as an executable script without compilation or build tools. By adding a shebang line (#!/usr/bin/env -S java --source 25), an instance void main() method using IO.println(), and making the file executable, you can create a system-wide runnable script in just 4 lines \u2014 no .java extension required.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d365e8cabb5d95ba36aaa092c23f211d?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-26T03:31:55.850Z"},{"id":"rDT3jp0Wb","title":"adam bien's blog","url":"https://adambien.blog/roller/abien/entry/145th_airhacks_tv_bce_airails_dev_zero_dependency_agents_","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/adam-bien-s-blog-rdt3jp0wb","summary":"Recap of the 145th AirHacks TV episode covering a range of Java and AI topics: the BCE (Boundary-Control-Entity) architectural pattern, zero-dependency Java 25 tooling (Agent Smith framework in ~130KB JAR, ZUnit test runner, ZB build tool), a zero-dependency MCP server, GPU-accelerated local LLM execution via TornadoVM with Apple Metal support for Mistral and DevStral, and the argument that LLMs understand standards better than frameworks enabling lean code generation. Also previews upcoming AirHacks Live workshops on spec-driven Java development.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d365e8cabb5d95ba36aaa092c23f211d?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-25T06:32:00.635Z"},{"id":"ZAZtp0Zyx","title":"adam bien's blog","url":"https://adambien.blog/roller/abien/entry/airails_dev_skills__transactional_in_bce_hibernate_validator_zero_framework_mcp_server_gpullama3_and_zsmith_agent_news_145th_airhacks_tv_","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/adam-bien-s-blog-zaztp0zyx","summary":"Agenda for the 145th airhacks.tv episode covering Java and Jakarta EE topics: @Transactional usage in BCE (Boundary-Control-Entity) architecture for bulk processing and API calls, structuring BCE in Jakarta Faces apps, local LLM inference with GPULlama3.java, alternatives to quarkus-hibernate-validator, a zero-framework MCP server implementation in Java 21, and updates on the zSmith agent and zeeds Java zero-dependency seed scripts.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d365e8cabb5d95ba36aaa092c23f211d?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-20T12:46:56.464Z"},{"id":"YNJYsd19e","title":"adam bien's blog","url":"https://adambien.blog/roller/abien/entry/early_2026_upcoming_conferences_workshops_and_events","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/adam-bien-s-blog-ynjysd19e","summary":"Adam Bien's upcoming conference talks and workshops schedule for 2026, covering topics like creating Java code with LLMs and agents, spec-driven Java development, LLM-assisted web components without frameworks, and escaping Java bloat by focusing on business logic first. Events span JCON Europe, Devoxx Greece, JAX Mainz, VibeKode Conference, and online workshops.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d365e8cabb5d95ba36aaa092c23f211d?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-18T09:34:49.562Z"},{"id":"ZhafB9kzG","title":"adam bien's blog","url":"https://adambien.blog/roller/abien/entry/java_25_script_files_with_classpath_in_the_shebang","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/adam-bien-s-blog-zhafb9kzg","summary":"Java 25 introduces script files via JEP 512 that are self-contained but also support specifying a classpath directly in the shebang line, allowing external JARs like zcl.jar to be referenced.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d365e8cabb5d95ba36aaa092c23f211d?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-09T12:53:44.418Z"},{"id":"L33CRR8cH","title":"adam bien's blog","url":"https://adambien.blog/roller/abien/entry/zunit_zero_dependency_java_25_test_runner","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/adam-bien-s-blog-l33crr8ch","summary":"zunit is a zero-dependency, single-file test runner for Java 25 that discovers *Test.java files and runs them directly via `java --source 25`. No compilation step, no JUnit, and no build tool is needed. Each test is a self-contained script with a `void main()` method, and each gets its own JVM for full execution isolation. The project is open source on GitHub.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d365e8cabb5d95ba36aaa092c23f211d?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-08T06:51:03.171Z"},{"id":"63s5eE2cY","title":"adam bien's blog","url":"https://adambien.blog/roller/abien/entry/how_to_quickly_switch_between","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/adam-bien-s-blog-63s5ee2cy","summary":"A quick tip for switching between JDK versions on macOS using shell aliases. By defining a bash alias that sets JAVA_HOME and updates PATH, developers can instantly switch to a specific Java version (e.g., Java 8) from the terminal without any additional tooling.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d365e8cabb5d95ba36aaa092c23f211d?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-16T06:58:05.790Z"},{"id":"6dOAnJYQZ","title":"adam bien's blog","url":"https://adambien.blog/roller/abien/entry/java_continuations_and_how_rife","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/adam-bien-s-blog-6doanjyqz","summary":"An airhacks.fm podcast episode featuring Geert Bevin discussing the creation of the Rife web framework using continuations in Java, refactoring to Java 17, and Java productivity improvements.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d365e8cabb5d95ba36aaa092c23f211d?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-16T06:58:05.624Z"}],"similar_handles":["securelist","csoonline","vespa","stackov","doccc"],"opposite_handles":["horde","dailydevworld","watercooler","on_leuwcq","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"securelist","handle":"securelist","name":"Securelist","is_squad":false,"x":-4.6748,"y":-5.1706,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":340,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/e4b9f556af7a4e74a179787362dd5b07","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":1.393444,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":10.523529,"tag_diversity":0.35},"top_tags_preview":[["cyber",247],["malware",203],["security",143]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-5.9706,-1.8235],"cadence_depth":[7.0147,6.6176],"hype_variety":[-5.3088,0.0441],"title_style":[1.7206,0.1912]}},{"id":"csoonline","handle":"csoonline","name":"CSO Online","is_squad":false,"x":-4.0462,"y":-5.1795,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":546,"image":"https:/